Attribution notes

The name Nurse Ratchet refers to the character in One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest:
the figure who administers care as control, in a register reasonable enough that
the coercion is difficult to point at. The name is the warning, not the aspiration.

ELIZA is a SEPARATE project in the Azazael tree -- the forensic investigation
suite -- with its own package and its own release gate. It is not this package.

Separately, the name ELIZA also refers to Joseph Weizenbaum's 1966 program
(Communications of the ACM, 9(1):36-45). No code from that program is included
here; that reference is to the cautionary lesson about systems that are trusted
because they appear to listen.

The crisis resources named in `nurse_ratchet/psyche/rt_agent.py` (988 Suicide & Crisis
Lifeline, US) are quoted as public information. This project is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or acting on behalf of that service or any health provider.

The labelled corpus in `nurse_ratchet/psyche/data/triage_corpus.jsonl` contains invented
utterances authored for this project. It contains no transcript, quotation or
paraphrase of any real person's words, and it must not be treated as a clinical
instrument or as a validation set.

No third-party runtime dependency is bundled. The Contributor Covenant text in
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is used under CC BY 4.0 with attribution retained in the
Attribution section at the end of that file.
